-- title:
--   No nontrivial coefficient lies in a unimodular normal closure
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a group and $w\in A*\langle t\rangle$ an element whose exponent sum in $t$ is $1$ or $-1$. If $g\in A$ lies in the normal closure of $w$, then
--   $$
--   g=1 .
--   $$
--
--   This is the Kervaire conjecture in its unimodular form, stated through the normal closure of the relator.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/GroupTheory/Kervaire/Main.lean#L41-L82

